.TH EQNORBITAL 2
.SH NAME
eqnorbital \- orbital-model harness for command-module Danby models
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B /dis/temple/eqnorbital.dis
.I model.dis
[
.I manual
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
A sibling to
.IR orbital (2)
for models that are ordinary command modules (an
.B init
plus an in-process
.B run(argv):
.RI ( string , int )
seam, matching
.IR hoc (2)'s
own already-established convention - see
.IR danby-aerobraking (1))
rather than plugins implementing
.IR orbital (2)'s
own bespoke
.B Model
.IR adt .
.B Eqnorbital
loads
.I model.dis
and calls its
.BR run(nil) ,
which returns the model's own spec as plain text - the model's whole
physics, printed, not compiled Limbo arithmetic reachable only through
a typed interface. There is no separate parsing module either:
.I this
file is the one place that actually drives a model, so it reads and
evaluates the spec directly.
.SS "The spec's own little language"
One directive per line:
.TP
.BI "title " TEXT
Rest of the line, verbatim.
.TP
.BI "bodylabels " "WORD ..."
.TP
.BI "mass " "NUM ..."
One value per
.BR bodylabels
word, same order.
.TP
.BI "param " LABEL " " DEFAULT " " MIN " " MAX
Repeatable.
.TP
.BI "maxtime " NUM
.TP
.BI "state " NAME " " EXPR ...
Repeatable; declares one named state variable. Its position among all
.B state
lines is its index in the eventual state/derivative arrays.
.I EXPR
is its initial value, an
.IR eqn (7)
expression that may reference any
.BR param 's
own name.
.TP
.BI "derivative " NAME " " EXPR ...
Repeatable, exactly one per
.B state
line, matched by
.IR NAME
(any order).
.I EXPR
may reference any state's own name, any param, or any
.BR eq .
.TP
.BI "eq " NAME " " EXPR ...
Repeatable; a named intermediate quantity, evaluated in declaration
order before every
.BR derivative ,
so a later
.B eq
or any
.B derivative
may reference an earlier
.B eq
by name.
.TP
.BI "observable " LABEL " " EXPR ...
Repeatable; same binding as
.BR derivative / eq .
Exactly two required - the shared client always plots two diagnostics
against time, the same requirement
.IR orbital (2)
already has.
.PP
Every
.I EXPR
is
.IR eqn (7)
syntax (see
.IR eqn2hoc (2)),
translated to
.IR hoc (2)
source and compiled ONCE, when the model is loaded; every simulation
step only rebinds symbols and evaluates the already-compiled trees.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/temple/eqnorbital.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR orbital (2)
(the original interface and harness, unmodified - the other 11
Orbital plugins still use it),
.IR eqn2hoc (2),
.IR hoc (2),
.IR danby-aerobraking (1),
.IR eqnorbitaltest (1)
.SH BUGS
No model using this harness has more than one moving body yet
(aerobraking's own "planet" body is fixed at the origin) - the spec
format allows any number of
.B state
lines, but nothing has exercised real N-body coupling through it.
